<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani yarn rates end down, seen steady.</title>
<headline>Pakistani yarn rates end down, seen steady.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates ended lower on Wednesday and are likely to remain stable around current levels owing to steady conditions in the domestic cotton market, dealers said.</p>
<p>Rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchants Association for a 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Wednesday    Previous</p>
<p>    Al-Karam (A.K.)	    485	    490</p>
<p>    Shafiq (Gold ky.)	  450	    470</p>
<p>    Globe (Hina)		 480	    490</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
